.SH NAME
anpu-watch - Keep watching a site, report only new problems


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu watch  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
watch runs repeated scans against a target on a fixed interval and
emits only findings that are new or changed since the previous scan.

.PP
Identity model: each iteration compares with \fBdiff.Compare\fR
(DedupKey identity, like \fBanpu diff\fR), but only \fIadded\fP
findings at/above the severity gate notify — changed/removed findings
are shown, not alerted. For pin-guarded baseline checks in CI, use
\fBanpu drift\fR (stable-ID identity + parser pins) instead.

.PP
The first run establishes a baseline. Every subsequent run diffs against
the previous completed scan (rolling comparison), so output stays quiet
until something actually changes. For a pinned baseline that never
moves, use \fBanpu drift\fR instead.

.PP
Examples:
  anpu watch https://staging.example.com
  anpu watch https://staging.example.com --interval 1h --min-confidence medium
  anpu watch https://staging.example.com --fail-on high --interval 30m


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--auto-install\fP[=false]
	auto-install missing external tools mid-scan instead of skipping them

.PP
\fB--cron\fP=""
	cron schedule for scans, e.g. "0 * * * *" (hourly); overrides --interval

.PP
\fB--discord\fP=""
	Discord webhook URL for fan-out diff notifications

.PP
\fB--fail-on\fP="none"
	exit non-zero if a new finding at or above this severity is found

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for watch

.PP
\fB--interval\fP=0s
	time between scans (e.g. 30m, 1h, 6h); 0 = run once then exit

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print diff results as JSON instead of the default text format

.PP
\fB--min-confidence\fP="none"
	skip findings below this confidence level

.PP
\fB--profile\fP="advanced"
	scan profile: safe, advanced, ultra (standard and deep are accepted aliases)

.PP
\fB--scope-file\fP=""
	allowlist file; off-scope targets abort before any request

.PP
\fB--telegram\fP=""
	Telegram botToken:chatID for fan-out diff notifications

.PP
\fB--webhook\fP=""
	URL to POST diff results to after each scan (Slack or generic JSON)

.PP
\fB--webhook-on\fP="change"
	when to send webhook notifications: always, change, finding

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	assume yes for install confirmations


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


